rapahoe, CO; Denver, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e91bcfa7a1cf8a1854d17bc85ccf3b07941aa5b5.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e91bcfa7a1cf8a1854d17bc85ccf3b07941aa5b5.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued August 13 at 3:49PM MDT until August 13 at 6:45PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Urban area and small stream flooding caused by excessive\nrainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Central Arapahoe County in northeastern Colorado...\nSouth Central Denver County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 645 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\nPonding of water in urban or other areas is occurring or is\nimminent.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 349 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges\nindicated heavy rain due to thunderstorms. This may cause urban\nand small stream flooding. Between 0.5 and 1 inch of rain has\nfallen.\n\n- Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1.5 inches are expected\nover the area. This additional rain will result in minor\nflooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nDenver, western Aurora, Greenwood Village, Cherry Hills Village\nand Cherry Creek Reservoir.","ends":"2026-08-13T18:45:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Arapahoe, CO; Denver, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2b81f09d20dc49285d0a0d95f067f79b997e960e.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2b81f09d20dc49285d0a0d95f067f79b997e960e.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-14T00:27:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 140027 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 627 PM MDT Thu Aug 13 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Localized flash flooding possible due to heavy rain producing thunderstorms. Highest risk is over the eastern Colorado plains, where a Flood Watch is in effect from 3 pm to 10 pm. - Another round of storms Friday afternoon/evening with a continued th